{
  "info": {
    "name": "RideLink – Account Service",
    "description": "IT3130 Application Development | Group Assignment\nMicroservice #1: Account & Authentication Service (Member 1)\n\nCovers:\n1. 🔐 Authentication & Token Management (Register, Login, Token Refresh, Logout)\n2. 👤 User Profile Management (Get Profile, PATCH/PUT Profile)\n3. 🔑 Admin User Operations (Get All Users, Query Filtering, Get by ID, Status Update, Admin Delete)\n4. 🗑️ Account Deletion (Self Delete & Verification)\n5. ❌ Negative & Error Scenarios (400 Bad Request, 401 Unauthorized, 403 Forbidden, 404 Not Found, 409 Conflict)\n\nCompliance:\n• IT3130 Lecture 07: REST Fundamentals (Resource URLs, HTTP semantics, Path vs Query, Status codes)\n• IT3130 Lecture 08: REST Constraints, Stateless JWT, Richardson Maturity Model Level 2\n\nHow to use:\n1. Import this collection into Postman\n2. Import the RideLink_Account_Environment.json environment file and select it\n3. Run requests individually or run the entire collection via Postman Collection Runner — variables chain automatically.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8081",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "🔐 1. Authentication & Token Management",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register – Passenger",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "    const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.environment.set('accessToken', json.accessToken);",
                  "    pm.environment.set('refreshToken', json.refreshToken);",
                  "    pm.environment.set('userId', json.userId);",
                  "    console.log('✅ Passenger registered. Token saved.');",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test('Status is 201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('Response has accessToken', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.have.property('accessToken'));",
                  "pm.test('Role is PASSENGER', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().role).to.eql('PASSENGER'));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"firstName\": \"Kamal\",\n  \"lastName\": \"Perera\",\n  \"email\": \"kamal.perera@test.com\",\n  \"password\": \"password123\",\n  \"phone\": \"0712345678\",\n  \"role\": \"PASSENGER\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "auth", "register"]}
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Register – Driver",
          "event": [
